  "n_shared_qids_supplied": 16,
  "n_shared_in_paired": 16,
  "rule": "the duplicate-photo structure is a property of VIZWIZ VAL ITSELF, 34 groups of byte-identical photos under different filenames, so it was present on BOTH sides. The exclusion is therefore applied to BOTH columns or NEITHER: excluding from the cloud column alone would compare a cleaned column against an uncleaned one, an asymmetry introduced by the cleaning rather than by the data.",
  "order_check": "the device ran in EXACT manifest order for both datasets, verified: manifest qid sequence == device row sequence, 4,319 of 4,319 for VizWiz and 700 of 700 for EgoThink. 'Repeats an image seen earlier' depends on order, so if the cloud also ran manifest order the candidate set is the SAME 52 and the matched exclusion is exact rather than a union. The cloud's order must be confirmed from its run meta.",
  "identifier_dedup_would_have_missed_this": "by image ID VizWiz val is 4,319 unique on 4,319 and passes clean. The duplicates are in file CONTENT under different filenames, and a cache keyed by content does not care what the identifier says. Identifier-based deduplication cannot see this class at all; the stronger form, hashing file contents, is what found it."
 },
